   "subject": "Hexagon shaped geom that acts like geom_point?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-NZ\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Hi<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Is there a way that I can in effect have a point geom that is shaped as a hexagon?  Either by some parameter to geom_point, or by tricking geom_hex away from\r\n its default stat_binhex?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">As an example attempt at the latter approach, the code below will place hexagons where I want to (correctly mapping x and y aesthetics) but I can’t override the\r\n stat_binhex treatment of size and fill – so I get uniform sized and grey coloured hexagons rather than ones with size and colour reflecting the z and w variables. \r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">I also tried an argument stat=”identity” in the geom_hex() function and that didn’t work either<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#1f497d\">dat &lt;- data.frame(<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#1f497d\">x = rnorm(100),<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#1f497d\">y = 3 + 4 *x + rnorm(100),<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#1f497d\">z =rnorm(100),<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-indent:36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#1f497d\">w=rnorm(100))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#1f497d\">ggplot(dat, aes(x=x, y=y, size=z, fill=w)) +\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#1f497d\">     geom_hex()<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Many thanks<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">PE</span><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u><u></u></span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p><font face=\"Verdana\" size=\"1\"><a href=\"http://newzealand.govt.nz/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://newzealand.govt.nz/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792374264384000&amp;usg=AOvVaw14u_HKPPTRoRkriWhT4ml8\">newzealand.govt.nz</a> - <font color=\"gray\">connecting you to New Zealand central &amp; local government \r\nservices</font> </font><br><br>\r\n<hr>\r\nAny opinions expressed in this message are not necessarily those of the Ministry \r\nof Business, Innovation and Employment. This message and any files transmitted \r\nwith it are confidential and solely for the use of the intended recipient. If \r\nyou are not the intended recipient or the person responsible for delivery to the \r\nintended recipient, be advised that you have received this message in error and \r\nthat any use is strictly prohibited. Please contact the sender and delete the \r\nmessage and any attachment from your computer. \r\n<hr>\r\n</p></div>\r\n\r\n"
